But you know what's even more suspicious?

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:35.840
The only teeth he has are his top front teeth,

00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:38.640
which should be coming in after his bottom front teeth.

00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:39.920
Now, it's not impossible,

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:41.520
but it's definitely very odd.

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:44.000
And it tells me that something here isn't quite right.

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:45.200
After doing a bit of research,

00:13:45.200 --> 00:13:46.880
if you see a kid who's JJ's age

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:48.160
without a majority of their teeth,

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:50.480
while it is possible they might just not have come in yet,

00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:52.160
there is another possibility.

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:53.600
A darker possibility.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:54.800
That they have come in

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:56.000
and have since fallen out

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:57.360
before they were supposed to.

00:13:57.360 --> 00:13:59.360
That might seem like an extreme conclusion to jump to,

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:01.680
but this actually isn't something all that impossible

00:14:01.680 --> 00:14:03.120
or uncommon in children.

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:04.480
In fact, it's a well-known disorder

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:06.400
known as hypophosphatasia,

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:08.160
or just HPP for short.

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:10.480
And it's not something that I would wish on anyone.

00:14:10.480 --> 00:14:11.920
HPP is a metabolic disease

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:13.600
that disrupts the development of bones.

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:17.040
And sadly, it can affect roughly 1 in 100,000 newborns.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:19.440
Basically, it disrupts a process called mineralization,

00:14:19.440 --> 00:14:21.200
where minerals like calcium and phosphorus

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:22.880
are deposited into bones and teeth.

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:24.000
Without this crucial step,

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:25.680
bones just won't develop properly,

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:26.720
causing them to become weak

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:28.000
and stunting the child's growth.

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:29.760
It can also cause your teeth to break

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:31.200
or fall out prematurely,

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:33.760
exactly what we might be seeing here with JJ.

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:34.400
The lost teeth?

00:14:34.400 --> 00:14:36.080
It's not the only sign that we can point to

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:37.360
regarding this diagnosis.

